$NetBSD$

Give configure.in the same machine= change patch-configure makes to the
generated configure, so that the two agree and a rerun of autoconf does not
undo it.  mips NetBSD was pointed at m/pmax.h, the DECstation description;
patch-src_m_mips.h puts a usable m/mips.h in its place.

This patch used to carry a second section against configure as well, with a
"+++ configure" line and no "--- configure.orig" above it.  patch took it, but
a patch named for one file that edits two is a trap: which of the two patches
touching configure wins then depends on the order the names sort in.  That
hunk now lives in patch-configure, where it belongs, and this patch touches
configure.in and nothing else.

--- configure.in.orig	2009-09-13 10:00:15.000000000 +0900
+++ configure.in
@@ -278,9 +278,9 @@ dnl see the `changequote' comment above.
       m68k-*-netbsd*)
 			# This is somewhat bogus.
 			machine=hp9000s300 ;;
-      mips-*-netbsd*)	machine=pmax ;;
-      mipsel-*-netbsd*)	machine=pmax ;;
-      mipseb-*-netbsd*)	machine=pmax ;;
+      mips-*-netbsd*)	machine=mips ;;
+      mipsel-*-netbsd*)	machine=mips ;;
+      mipseb-*-netbsd*)	machine=mips ;;
       ns32k-*-netbsd*)	machine=ns32000 ;;
       powerpc-*-netbsd*) machine=macppc ;;
       sparc*-*-netbsd*)	machine=sparc ;;
